{"title":"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bobby is bored one day and flips a fair coin until it lands on tails. Bobby wins if the coin lands on heads a positive even number of times in the sequence of tosses. The probability that Bobby wins can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bag is big enough to hold exactly 6 large pencils, 12 medium pencils, or 30 small pencils, with no space left over. Given that there is 1 large pencil and 3 medium pencils currently in the bag, what is the maximum number of small pencils that may be added to the bag?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a parallelogram such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de9e04a11abd6c01a5d47091e8ab685128014fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CE}{DE}=\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"39\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58cf2c01b32821ad23584e33cc96ba86963d7961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49fb2b3b658e839330eeec052f81d51f780a587f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB+CD=AD+BC=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"229\" height=\"16\" />. There exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in 3D space such that the distances from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are all equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Find the volume of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a01f6c60a4a9d15a82c214ca37f0df9fdc371ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a square such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c1a3727993adf8d4a4833757fc6db7010e96af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c41044b564108bc3fd60ac4f6e84d80bd72c5b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[BEF]}{[ABCD]}=\\frac{7}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"121\" height=\"45\" />, then the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1dfeb57e09dccb79f36781029eceecbe2bbd47ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{EF^2}{BC^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"41\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the beginning of day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there is a single bacterium in a petri dish. During each day, each bacterium in the petri dish divides into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8726d98aced2f3140dd77a2d8614c2e7674700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> new bacteria, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cca117c11e298720e03826725b6d317e21ef64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> bacteria are added to the petri dish. For example, at the end of day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> bacteria in the petri dish. If, at the end of day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the number of bacteria in the petri dish is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, find the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f2056ab10712daa9982746decb50985e30de67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=(1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6fe064a91d4c95bec89cd8c80ac9800c188e548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> as the image of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> under a rotation of either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d3f11ab7a3e93c7a404a34224228f0449505a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54930ee3937d1087e4262a992f6770c261947e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$135^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> clockwise about the origin, with each choice having a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance of being selected. Find the expected value of the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> coincides with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive integers cannot be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e6825582a17ca6244d419f239fc399babcbc7e1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7a + 19b + 28c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers (not necessarily distinct)?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde1774a06facbf7b3c05e82bc4ed9bd41cd786a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace7328133fbaac6396a6e5fc9fa65f335320cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a20686d6a518df9865b1b3d8abb870bdeaad690f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and a square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5ae853879661bccaf47712a492ec2decc8fab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/8820cdb9ddec09011a25ab50173aa7cd580c8240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{AB}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"22\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c61d1f9fc3301e4c2a574a35b2310dc8131849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{CA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"21\" />. Suppose further that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> are distinct from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then the sum of all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/493f254f8bfca6c8153a43bd98c125ea95e0029f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BP}{CP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"31\" height=\"37\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a49696e74b8b660b8c2f4cbcfde366378b5141a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{2,7,15,26,\\ldots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" /> be the set of all numbers for which the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6934c6c653b822d4b861f82307a28c4b4bb1df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> element in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6934c6c653b822d4b861f82307a28c4b4bb1df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> triangular number and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6934c6c653b822d4b861f82307a28c4b4bb1df3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> positive perfect square. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the set which contains all unique remainders when the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Find the number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 SSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018064516\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 505/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16697/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24522:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018064516 and revision id 280